	<https://linked.archi/examples/vio/concepts#customer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Travel agencies are trade partners (B2B), not customers. The lead passenger who books and pays is the booker; every traveller on the booking is a customer. A source market is an organisation unit, not a customer segment."@en ;
		<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A traveller who buys a VIO holiday, directly or through a trade partner."@en ;
		<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "booker"@en , "guest"@en , "traveller"@en , "client"@en ;
